</code></pre>

Q: What is best practice when an expressions is required in signal forms [formField]? A: <p>Do not put expressions inside <code>[formField]</code>. <code>[formField]</code> expects a <strong>Signal Forms field, not the field value</strong></p>
<p>Wrong - <code>&lt;input matInput [formField]=&quot;toDisplayString(formModel.myenum().value)&quot;/&gt;</code><br />
Correct -  <code>&lt;input matInput [formField]=&quot;form.myenumDisplayString&quot; /&gt;</code></p>
<p>In formModel</p>
<pre><code>interface MyFormModel {
  myenum: MyEnum;
  myenumDisplayString: string;
}
</code></pre>
<p>mapper</p>
<pre><code>dtoToFormModel(dto: MyDto): MyFormModel {
  return {
    myenum: dto.myenum,
    myenumDisplayString: toDisplayString(dto.myenum),
  };
}
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> If it is only for display, <strong>better use a computed value and do not use [formField]</strong></p>
</blockquote>
